<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Auguste Pavie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1847–1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Auguste Pavie was a French explorer and diplomat who mapped much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. As French vice-consul at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a>, he rescued King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oun-kham">Oun Kham</a> when Chinese Haw raiders sacked the city in 1887, winning the loyalty of the court. His work prepared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-siamese-war">Franco-Siamese crisis of 1893</a>, after which the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> became the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of Laos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/auguste-pavie.jpg" alt="Auguste Pavie" width="200" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AJMPavie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
